menu "Alarm Clock (bedside alarm)"

    config ALARM_CLOCK_ENABLED
        bool "Enable bedside alarm clock feature"
        default n
        help
            Adds a configurable alarm schedule (Web UI / Telegram) that wakes
            the device with no WiFi, photo rotation, or Agenda render, plays
            a repeating tone through the Chimes speaker, and can be stopped
            with a long KEY press - see docs/ALARMCLOCK_FEASIBILITY.md.

            Off by default and excluded from the build entirely rather than
            just hidden, since not every supported board can usefully act as
            a bedside alarm clock (no speaker, no buttons in the required
            shape, etc.) - enable via `build.py --alarmclock` rather than
            selecting this directly unless you know what you're doing.

endmenu
